 and  then I think these congressional  investigations I think the Senate side  feels pretty good about where they ended  last year that they focused a lot on  kind of the information aspect of  Russian influence online and social  media the house side is sort of starting  a bunch of new investigations I'm  relating more to the Trump family  finances potential foreign influence  beyond  Russia into the family and then a lot of  other questions that they feel are  unanswered lines of approach on the  Russia investigation so I think there is  this kind of initial core that was  hopefully I mean hopefully what what  eventually is known from Muller is the  here's some answers to some questions  about Russia but there's probably gonna  be a lot of other questions connected to  that and I think none of this will be  done anytime soon but we need to go  through I think every different aspect  of that to understand what happened in  2016 prevented from happening again and  really look more deeply at issues of  foreign influence and corruption in our  own political system so let's talk a  little bit about the Southern District  of New York  component and then I have a bunch of  other stuff to ask you about so when the  BuzzFeed news story came out asserting  that we had finally testimony in the  hands of robert muller from michael  cohen claiming specific actions were  directed by donald trump  there was a clarification or a statement  put out by a spokesperson for robert  muller that was pretty narrowly worded  and it said that some of the  characterizations in the article about  testimony given to the special counsel  are not actually in the possession of  the special counsel and one of the  interpretations was everything in the  story could be accurate except that it  was given to the Southern District of  New York and not to the special counsel  is that a possibility number one and  then just more generally what what is  this Southern District of New York what  is their 